menuconfig MESHTASTIC_LED_STATUS
	bool "Board LED reflects BLE peer-link state (bench diagnostic)"
	default n
	depends on GPIO
	depends on MESHTASTIC_BLE_PEER
	depends on !MESHTASTIC_EXTNOTIFY
	help
	  Drives led0 directly, independent of the Meshtastic app/config: solid
	  while powered with no active BLE peer link, 1 Hz blink (1 s on, 1 s
	  off) while at least one peer link — inbound or outbound — is up and
	  exchanging beats/notifications.

	  A bench-visibility aid for the node-to-node BLE peer link
	  (CONFIG_MESHTASTIC_BLE_PEER), built to answer "which of these boards
	  are actually meshing over Bluetooth right now" at a glance, without a
	  console open on every one of them.

	  Mutually exclusive with CONFIG_MESHTASTIC_EXTNOTIFY: both want sole
	  ownership of led0, and this module does not arbitrate with it. Turn
	  extnotify off in the same build to use this.

if MESHTASTIC_LED_STATUS

config MESHTASTIC_LED_STATUS_TICK_MS
	int "Poll/toggle tick (ms)"
	default 1000
	range 100 5000
	help
	  How often the peer-link state is checked, and — while meshing — the
	  half-period of the blink. 1000 ms gives the documented 1 s on / 1 s
	  off pattern. A shorter tick makes the "solid -> blink" transition
	  snappier at the cost of more frequent GPIO writes; both are cheap.

endif # MESHTASTIC_LED_STATUS
